  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HYDROLOGICAL RESTORATION &amp; WATERFOWL HAB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ra Celestn Biosphere Reserve is a mangrove area in the state of Campeche that has been degraded by a road built 35 years ago. To address this problem, the grantee began a mangrove restoration initiative in the northern portion of the Reserve in 2001, followed by work in the middle and southeastern portions. Their work accelerated the natural mangrove regeneration process by increasing the freshwater input into the system and reducing salinity. Studies have demonstrated improved survival and growth of seedlings and an increase in the density of mangrove trees. In this fourth phase of the project, the grantee will work in a new portion of the Reserve. This project will restore 2,025.4 acres of coastal wetlands within the Celestn Biosphere Reserve in the state of Campeche. It will also survey habitat quality, including salinity, hydroperiod, fisheries productivity, habitat use by waterfowl and other aquatic birds, and conduct a remote sensing analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
